# WolkaraForever layer patch 0073 - AppKit: the host keeps the layer's touch controls
#
# Why: Tolkara edc3628 rebuilt its own on-screen controls (translation/AppKit/TouchControls.m:
# a row or side columns with a movement stick, Shift, key buttons and a camera mode) and
# taught the AppKit host to lay them out: it moves the controls into a container beside the
# game, shrinks the game between their columns (AKTouchLayoutFor, AKScreenSetGameSize) and
# hides the drawn pointer in their camera mode. The layer replaces that TouchControls with its
# own (wolkaraforever/Touch/TouchControls.m, overlaid), as it did before the update: a toolbar
# over the game that places itself, reads the touches landing on the host view, and has no
# columns, stick or camera mode. Left as upstream wrote it, the host does not compile against
# the layer's controls, and if it did it would move them out of the view whose touches they
# read.
#
# What it does: the host adds the layer's controls to itself exactly as before the update,
# keeps the whole container for the game, and draws the pointer the trackpad moves. Upstream's
# container view, raw-pointer path and every other host change stay. The AppKit view suite's
# assertions about the platform's own controls (column layouts, stick, Shift, key buttons, the
# four-button row) are removed; the layer's controls have their own suites.
#
# Applies after: 0060-host-multitouch-contract-per-interface.patch
# Applies to: translation/AppKit/AppKit.m, tests/test_appkit_views.m
# Upstream: not a candidate - it exists because the layer replaces upstream's controls.
#

